//? Title: CRNN and CTC: visible tensor word recognition
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A cropped word image must become a variable-length string without character boundaries. Convolutional features and bidirectional recurrence produce an unaligned time sequence;CTC sums its feasible label paths. Hand path/Jacobian examples precede complete graph checks,real human word crops,visible Adam and restored image-only inference,with every held-out transcription error reported.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.8_other_vision_tasks/crnn_ctc.cpp`.

> The method

The fixed observed crop is32x100 grayscale. Seven convolutional stages turn
its width into26 sequence positions;two projected bidirectional LSTMs supply
37 class logits at each position. CTC marginalizes time alignments for the
true variable-length word. Greedy decoding selects each time’s class before
collapsing repeats/blanks,so it need not maximize total target-word mass.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/crnn_ctc_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/crnn_ctc_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/crnn_ctc_concept.tikz > build/crnn_ctc_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/crnn_ctc_concept.svg build/crnn_ctc_concept.dvi > build/crnn_ctc_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
