\image(figures/crnn_ctc_repeats.svg)
// result_end
\caption(The complete3x3 class-probability and CTC-adjoint maps for a repeated target. Class2 is the blank;time0 is at the bottom. Native enumeration independently checks every logit derivative.)
\alttext(The complete3x3 class-probability and CTC-adjoint maps for a repeated target. Class2 is the blank;time0 is at the bottom. Native enumeration independently checks every logit derivative.)

> Sum alignments instead of selecting one path

For a one-character target and two steps,the paths[0,0],[0,blank] and
[blank,0] all contribute. If the character probability is p at both times,
with only a negligible third-class mass,the target probability approaches
\(p^2+2p(1-p)=2p-p^2\). At p=.5,this is .75,not the .25 probability of
one particular path. Greedy path decoding and best target-word probability
therefore answer different questions.
```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/crnn_ctc_marginal.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  const auto p = n::arange(.01, .9901, .01, n::DType::Float64);
  const auto epsilon = n::full(p.shape(), 1e-8, n::DType::Float64), word = (1. - epsilon) * p,
             blank = (1. - epsilon) * (1. - p);
  const auto logits =
      n::tile(n::expand_dims(n::log(n::stack({word, epsilon, blank}, 1)), 0), {2, 1, 1})
          .to(n::DType::Float32);
  const auto labels = n::zeros({p.numel(), 1}, n::DType::Int32),
             length = n::ones({p.numel()}, n::DType::Int32),
             time = n::full({p.numel()}, 2, n::DType::Int32);
  const auto marginal =
                 n::exp(-n::ctc_loss(logits, labels, length, time)).to(n::DType::Float64),
             direct = word * word + 2. * word * blank;
  const double error = n::max(n::abs(marginal - direct)).item();
  if (error > 2e-7)
    return 1;
  auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.lines(p.to_vector<double>(), marginal.to_vector<double>(), "all3 paths", {37, 99, 235})
      .lines(p.to_vector<double>(), n::square(word).to_vector<double>(), "path[0,0]",
             {220, 38, 38})
      .title("Three alignments share one target")
      .x_label("character probability at each time")
      .y_label("target/path probability")
      .y_limits(0, 1.25)
      .size(950, 480);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  plot.save_svg("build/crnn_ctc_marginal.svg");
  std::print("99 CTC marginal probabilities agree with independent three-term formula,max "
             "error {:.3g}. At p=.5,all-path mass approaches.75 versus.25 for one path.\n",
             error);
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
99 CTC marginal probabilities agree with independent three-term formula,max error 4.21e-08. At p=.5,all-path mass approaches.75 versus.25 for one path.
\image(figures/crnn_ctc_marginal.svg)
