\caption(Eighteen visible Adam minibatch updates train all convolutional/recurrent parameters. Paired BN restoration is selected by validation CTC;the printed word errors remain the test of recognition.)
\alttext(Eighteen visible Adam minibatch updates train all convolutional/recurrent parameters. Paired BN restoration is selected by validation CTC;the printed word errors remain the test of recognition.)


\image(figures/crnn_ctc_blank.svg)
\caption(The selected model’s blank probability across all26 time steps for the first held-out crop. This exposes how a lower CTC objective can coexist with empty greedy words.)
\alttext(Blank-class probability over the first actual held-out word’s CRNN sequence.)

\image(figures/crnn_ctc_predictions.png)
\caption(All six actual held-out word crops,two per row,in the printed prediction table’s order. The labels are human annotations and predictions may be empty;this figure does not synthesize successful recognition.)
\alttext(Real held-out COCO-Text word crops with their true and decoded words listed immediately above.)

All six selected test words decode to empty strings:0/6 exact and CER1
(27 deletions/27 reference characters),equal to the empty-string reference.
The initial model has31 edits/CER1.148148. Eighteen updates reduce full
fitting CTC78.655991->36.410206 and select epoch3 validation CTC33.693634,
without establishing useful word recognition.

A few epochs on43 cropped words are insufficient evidence for useful scene
text recognition. CTC optimization,greedy word accuracy and character edit
rate answer different questions. Original-box assistance,three test source
photographs,grayscale stretching and lack of pretraining sharply limit the
experiment. No text-detection or benchmark-accuracy claim is made.

> Conclusion

Exhaustive path values and every adjoint establish the CTC mechanism before fitting. Complete convolution/recurrent graphs and auditable human crops then support visible tensor optimization. Paired-state image-only deployment is immutable;actual decoded words expose how short training can reduce loss without learning useful recognition.

> References

- [Shi,Bai and Yao(2015),An End-to-End Trainable Neural Network for Image-based Sequence Recognition and Its Application to Scene Text Recognition](https://arxiv.org/abs/1507.05717).
- [Graves et al.(2006),Connectionist Temporal Classification](https://www.cs.toronto.edu/~graves/icml_2006.pdf).
- [Veit et al.(2016),COCO-Text:Dataset and Benchmark for Text Detection and Recognition in Natural Images](https://arxiv.org/abs/1601.07140).
- [COCO-Text V2 official annotation release](https://github.com/bgshih/cocotext/releases/download/dl/cocotext.v2.zip).
